# Azure Integration Services Demo — request collection
#
# Runs in VS Code (REST Client) or JetBrains Rider. Fill the two variables from
# Terraform, then work down: the file follows SPEC.md 14 in presentation order.
#
#   cd infra
#   terraform output -raw gateway_url
#   terraform output -raw subscription_key
#
# @name is set on requests whose response feeds a later one, so order IDs
# thread through without copy-paste.

@gateway = https://apim-aisdemo-REPLACE.azure-api.net/orders-demo
@subscriptionKey = REPLACE_WITH_TERRAFORM_OUTPUT


###############################################################################
# 14.1  HAPPY PATH
#
# Accepted synchronously, processed asynchronously. Note the 202 rather than a
# 200: the gateway is not waiting for the work, and the Location header points
# at where the answer will appear.
###############################################################################

# @name happyPath
POST {{gateway}}/orders
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "CUST-1042",
  "customerName": "Contoso Ltd",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "WIDGET-01", "quantity": 3, "unitPrice": 249.99 }
  ]
}

### Poll until it reaches Completed. Run this two or three times in a row —
### the status walks Accepted -> Processing -> Completed.
GET {{gateway}}/orders/{{happyPath.response.body.orderId}}
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}


###############################################################################
# 14.2  FAN-OUT AND FILTERING
#
# One event, two independent subscribers, a SQL filter deciding delivery.
# The threshold is notification_threshold (default 500).
#
# The small order reaches AuditHandler only. The large one reaches both.
# Neither knows the other exists, and ProcessOrder knows about neither.
###############################################################################

# @name smallOrder
POST {{gateway}}/orders
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "CUST-SMALL",
  "customerName": "Below Threshold",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "TRINKET-01", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 50.00 }
  ]
}

###
# @name largeOrder
POST {{gateway}}/orders
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "CUST-LARGE",
  "customerName": "Above Threshold",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "MACHINE-01", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 5000.00 }
  ]
}

### Both complete. The difference is invisible here and visible in the
### telemetry — see demo/queries.kql, "who handled which event".
GET {{gateway}}/orders/{{largeOrder.response.body.orderId}}
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}


###############################################################################
# 14.3  POISON MESSAGE -> DEAD LETTER -> REPLAY
#
# simulateFailure makes ProcessOrder throw. Service Bus redelivers five times,
# then dead-letters.
#
# Watch the order row stall at Retrying with attemptCount 5. Nothing updates it
# after that: the message is in the dead-letter queue and no code is looking at
# it. That gap is the lesson, not a bug.
###############################################################################

# @name poisonOrder
POST {{gateway}}/orders
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "CUST-POISON",
  "customerName": "Poison Pill",
  "simulateFailure": true,
  "items": [
    { "sku": "WIDGET-01", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 99.00 }
  ]
}

### Poll this a few times over ~60s. It climbs to Retrying / attemptCount 5,
### carries the failure reason, and then stops changing entirely.
GET {{gateway}}/orders/{{poisonOrder.response.body.orderId}}
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}

### Drain the dead-letter queue and resubmit.
###
### Replay clears the injected failure switch, standing in for the remediation
### an operator would do first. Add ?remediate=false to replay it untouched and
### watch it dead-letter all over again — which is what replaying a genuinely
### broken message actually does.
POST {{gateway}}/admin/replay?max=10
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Now Completed, attemptCount back to 1, failureReason cleared.
GET {{gateway}}/orders/{{poisonOrder.response.body.orderId}}
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}


###############################################################################
# 14.4  MALFORMED MESSAGE
#
# Not runnable from here. It has to be injected straight onto the queue,
# bypassing the gateway, which needs a Service Bus data-plane token:
#
#   ./scripts/inject-malformed.ps1
#
# It fails at deserialization rather than in business logic, and dead-letters
# the same way. The contrast with the next section is the point: one kind of
# bad input the gateway catches, one kind it never sees.
###############################################################################


###############################################################################
# 14.5  GATEWAY REJECTION
#
# These never reach compute. No Function invocation appears in Application
# Insights for any of them — the gateway answered on its own.
###############################################################################

### No subscription key -> 401 at the gateway.
POST {{gateway}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "CUST-NOKEY",
  "items": [ { "sku": "W", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 10.00 } ]
}

### Invalid subscription key -> 401 at the gateway.
POST {{gateway}}/orders
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: not-a-real-key
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "CUST-BADKEY",
  "items": [ { "sku": "W", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 10.00 } ]
}

### Rate limiting is NOT part of this scenario on the Consumption tier, which
### permits no rate-limiting policy at all — rate-limit, rate-limit-by-key,
### quota, and quota-by-key are each rejected at deploy time. Set
### apim_sku_name to a paid tier and the policy appears automatically.
### See SPEC.md 5.1.1.

### Valid key, invalid body -> 400 from the function, in problem+json.
### The gateway let this through; the backend rejected it. Worth showing right
### after the 401s, because the two look similar to a caller and are decided in
### completely different places.
POST {{gateway}}/orders
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "",
  "items": []
}

### Unknown order -> 404 in problem+json.
GET {{gateway}}/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}


###############################################################################
# 14.6  BURST AND SCALE-OUT
#
# Not runnable from here either — it needs concurrency:
#
#   ./scripts/load-test.ps1 -Count 100
#
# Raise PROCESSING_DELAY_MS first (terraform apply -var processing_delay_ms=3000)
# so the queue visibly fills before it drains.
###############################################################################
